/TITLE
weldtool spot-weld shear smoke test
# STARTING POINT ONLY - VERIFY WITH TEST COUPONS before any structural or safety use.
# metal=mild-steel t=1.0 mm nugget d=4.000 mm (4.0*sqrt(t)) area=12.566 mm2
# F_shear=2.121 kN  F_normal=1.485 kN
# UTS 290 MPa from NSRW_LC (42 ksi lower bound, note 1)
# shear = AWS C1.1-AMD1 minimum shear-tension strength
# normal = 0.7 x shear (TWI lower-bound CTS/TSS for UTS 290 MPa)
# density 7850 kg/m3 (repo-wide steel assumption)
# E, G, failure displacements = Altair example values (ALTAIR_LAW59 / ALTAIR_FAILCONNECT example (Spotweld)): CALIBRATE with 0/90 deg, combined and peel tests
# Perfectly plastic yield curves (flat): a simplification, not data.
# Ifail=1 (coupled normal+shear failure) chosen as the conservative option; Altair example uses 0.
# Element: /BRICK + /PROP/TYPE43, tied to shells with /INTER/TYPE2 (not generated here).
/UNIT/1
unit for mat
